
Here are some tools for keeping supercomputers busy.

slaunch Job.sbatch 4

will launch 4 dependent instances of Job.sbatch.

It also launches a sidecar job for each one of these jobs,
to tar the result and plot every frame you made.

1.) put slaunch in your scripts directory.
2.) Copy Job.sbatch to your run directory.  Make it work for you.
3.) Put this repo in your repos, something like $HOME/repos/slaunch.
4.) Edit PlotAndTar.sbatch to point to the right tarme and plotme.  Or do something different.
5.) Feel free to make this better.


slaunch: the launcher. Put in your path.
Job.sbatch: put in your job site.  Edit to match your needs.  
            This error checks so a failed enzo doesn't run 500 times.
            Failed or completed runs write a file called NOGO
            If NOGO is present, neither slaunch or Job.sbatch will go.
            Keep an eye out for NOGO, it means its time to pay attention.
PlotAndTar.sbatch: The plot and tar script. Take a look, edit to your liking.
plotme: plots density with grid lines for every file.  
        If you leave the plots in their directories, they won't get remade.
        Stupid parallel, launching multiple instances of the script will 
        not fight each other.
tarme: the tar script.

      
